## Quick Reference

| Letter | Principle | Pattern Examples |
|--------|-----------|------------------|
| C | Compose | Decorator, Strategy, Builder, Functional Options |
| L | Layer purity | Hexagonal Architecture, Ports & Adapters, Clean Architecture |
| A | Architectural performance | Cache-aside, Index-first queries, ID pagination |
| R | Represent intent | Parameter Objects, Value Objects, Domain Types |
| I | Input guarded | Chain of Responsibility, Guard Pattern, Validation Pipeline |
| T | Telemetry first | Structured logging, Metrics, Distributed tracing |
| Y | Yield safe failure | Feature flags, Circuit breakers, Fallback strategies |

---

## Summary

**Golden Rule**: Code should read like a conversation in the domain language, be fast by design, safe by default, and observable everywhere.

CLARITY ensures that systems are:
- ✅ **Composable** (easy to extend)
- ✅ **Clear** (intent is obvious)
- ✅ **Correct** (validated inputs)
- ✅ **Fast** (architectural decisions)
- ✅ **Observable** (instrumented)
- ✅ **Resilient** (safe failure modes)
